{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Helsinki lags nationally in crude recorded MDT meetings (0.1%, 95% CI 0.0–0.4 vs 6.0%) and has lower crude symptomatic treatment (34.5%, 95% CI 32.1–37.0 vs 39.5%).",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Helsingin_kaupunki",
        "nat:mdt_recorded",
        "cty:symptomatic:Helsingin_kaupunki",
        "nat:symptomatic"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "In Helsinki, the crude share of patients with a recorded MDT meeting is 0.1% (95% CI 0.0–0.4; n=1/1486) compared with 6.0% (893/14873) nationally; the 95% confidence interval excludes the national value, though HILMO MDT codes measure recording practice from direct patient contacts rather than multidisciplinary care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping crude treatment categories that are not adjusted for age or stage, Helsinki's crude symptomatic share is 34.5% (95% CI 32.1–37.0; n=513/1486) versus 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally and crude curative share is 33.0% (95% CI 30.7–35.5; n=491/1486) versus 27.0% (4009/14873), with each 95% confidence interval excluding the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:symptomatic:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "cty:curative:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Helsinki's crude life-prolonging treatment share is 30.8% (95% CI 28.5–33.1; n=457/1486) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally, and its crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 29.1% (95% CI 26.8–31.4; n=432/1486) versus 27.5% (4089/14873); the 95% confidence intervals include the national values.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:no_treatment_record"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure county access times, but preliminary, unpublished national averages show lung cancer takes 155 days from symptom onset to treatment in Finland versus 107 in Sweden and 67 in Denmark, with 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Diagnosis counts are well supported, but crude county treatment shares lack age or stage adjustment, and public registry data do not capture pathway dates or pre-specialist care.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "lit:hilmo_90",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "\"No treatment record within 12 months\" mixes untreated patients and unrecorded treatment; as an inference from this data-quality signal, not a finding, Helsinki's crude 29.1% share (95% CI 26.8–31.4; n=432/1486) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally has a 95% confidence interval including 27.5%, though being above 27.5% means lower crude symptomatic share (34.5%, 95% CI 32.1–37.0) may partly reflect unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:symptomatic:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "County treatment shares are crude and not adjusted for age or stage: stage at diagnosis is missing for ~48% of new patients, and while Kuva 16 provides digitised national age-adjusted curative shares of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women (read off a figure, precision ±0.5 percentage points), no age-adjusted county value is provided.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article found HILMO diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, concerning diagnosis concordance only, while symptoms and referrals are not measured in public data, occupational health is not mentioned, and outpatient primary care visits are not included in the report's data.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data capture imaging only indirectly as the basis of diagnosis in approximately 20% of cases without imaging dates or waits, record whether a specialist visit occurred within 12 months (93.6% nationally) rather than when, and show treatment types within 12 months without treatment start dates.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends auditing stage, drug, and MDT recording completeness, reporting access times using THL 21/2016 definitions with handover alerts, and standardising referrals and diagnostic-phase contacts.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:950a2f797b",
        "q:556431a0c2"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Given Helsinki's 0.1% (95% CI 0.0–0.4; n=1/1486) crude recorded MDT share, 29.1% (95% CI 26.8–31.4; n=432/1486) crude no-treatment-record share, ~48% missing stage nationally, and incomplete national data collection, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while the roadmap plans a national quality registry targeting 90% coverage.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Helsingin_kaupunki",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because Health Care Act §52 sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion, the roadmap plans national pathway descriptions and target access times by 2026–2028, and the Filha diagnostics guideline is due before the 2030 mid-term evaluation, the team recommends reporting access times using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions (for 16 cancers) with handover alerts.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Since referrals follow local instructions and mentor insight notes weak referrals receive lower specialist urgency ratings, the team recommends a standard referral template, referring persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and naming a diagnostic-phase contact, while the roadmap plans standardised referral criteria and care-coordinator guidance by 2026–2028 (for county adoption by 2029–2031).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
